re : robbing shops

IMO:
Shopkeepers hate shoplifters, jealously value their inventory and only lot of
money can humor them. After being robbed, they only want your hide to add to
their collection of hides, also reposessing all your belongings. They leave
their shops seeking you liken to a heat(or is it meat)seeking missile because
you're the only thief around. Their policy is hit first and talk shop later.
If you survive all the poundings and gets your turn try "p" as in pay, and he
*might* just let you keep your hide. 
Kops, I think, can pick things up and leave (going after you) shops without 
paying. If you are equiped for kops and shopkeeper there is fun in this.
(orcs also steal without being persecuted)

Here is an interesting point: why don't you get procecuted instead of being
lynched by a mob of kops? Dungeons are like jailhouses right? And there is
a royal court(opulent throne room), and a septre being pounded in judgement!
This might give some much needed clues to the new hacker who then finds himself
in the castle being judged and sentence by the master lich or the Wiz of Y.
For instance:
"You have been apprehended for shoplifting"
"You appear before a royal court bound by 4 chains and balls."
"The Wizard, wearing the Amulet of Yendor, delivers the judgement -more- "
    "OFF with his HEAD!"
Getting caught happens only after your hp drops into negative (you goose is
already cook before you get to see the Wizard.)

Spoilers on robbing shops are often abound, catch one and take no risk!
Shopkeepers will not accept being paid Tuesday for a hamburger today!

Though, more seriously: If you ate food without paying, and your dog is in or
outside the shop regardless, the shopkeeper will not let you leave. He guards
the door longer than you can read the entire encycopedia Britainica twice 
backwards.However,this I haven't try, you might kick sideways to break the door
down so you can step *diagonally* into the "archway" of the door and escape
(with kops and one MAD shopkeeper in tow)
In sheer desparation, sell part or all your inventory to get $ to pay and leave.

